{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.InteriorMarkovOfBraidedTower"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.tr_pureBondChain_of_braided","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.tr_pureBondChain_of_braided","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L149-L156","doc":"**The general-`A` bond product on every braided tower.** No hypothesis\nbeyond the Iwahori–Hecke relations (quadratic, far-commutation, braid) and the\nMarkov axioms: the gap `MarkovBondFactor` names for general `A` is a theorem\nhere, in the `c_k = 1` shape every production bond type has. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.tr_pureBondChain_of_interiorMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.tr_pureBondChain_of_interiorMarkov","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L131-L141","doc":"**The general-`A` bond product, conditionally on `InteriorMarkov`.**\nFor strictly increasing bonds `g₀ < g₁ < ⋯`,\n`tr ((σ_{g₀} + d₀) * (σ_{g₁} + d₁) * ⋯) = ∏_k (z + d_k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.chainOK_pureChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.chainOK_pureChain","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L117-L129","doc":"A strictly increasing bond list gives a legal chain: every block is `1`, so\nthe `upper`/`H` memberships are `one_mem` and only the ordering has content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.Increasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.Increasing","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L111-L115","doc":"`Chain'`-style strict increase of the bond indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.freeWord_pureChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.freeWord_pureChain","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L104-L109","doc":"Deleting every bond from a pure chain leaves `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.map_pureChain_z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.map_pureChain_z","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L95-L101","doc":"The bond multipliers of a pure chain are the `d`'s it was built from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.pureChain_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.pureChain_cons","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.pureChain_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.pureChain_nil","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.pureChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.PureBondChainProduct.pureChain","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/PureBondChainProduct.lean#L82-L86","doc":"The bond chain with no blocks: bonds `gs` in order, every intervening block\n`1`. Paired with `bondWord … 1` this is the bare product\n`(σ_{g₀} + d₀) * (σ_{g₁} + d₁) * ⋯`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}